    "created_at": "2026-04-13T21:02:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-04-13T21:02:29Z",
    "body": "We've made some further progress on CSS Gaps 1, and I think there are some additional properties that should be included in the list alongside `row-rule-*`.\n\nOne thing I noticed about the list is that some of them are longhands and some are shorthands. For all of the gap and gap decoration related properties, we have parallel sets of properties that work in each direction (column and row), and shorthands that work in both directions simultaneously. For brevity and consistency I'd suggest we list the bi-directional shorthands only, and propose the following changes:\n\nAdd the following properties:\n* [gap](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-align-3/#gap-shorthand)\n* [grid-gap](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-align-3/#gap-legacy)\n* [rule](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-gaps-1/#gap-decoration-shorthands)\n* [rule-break](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-gaps-1/#break)\n* [rule-inset](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-gaps-1/#inset)\n* [rule-overlap](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-gaps-1/#overlap)\n* [rule-visibility-items](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-gaps-1/#visibility)\n\nAnd strike the following properties since they're covered by the above:\n* column-gap\n* column-rule\n* grid-column-gap\n* grid-row-gap\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
